# The screen drawn by four processors: after `cpu start` the console's
# lines and the copy to video memory are spread over all of them. What a
# monitor shows must be the same as with one.
@cpus 4
@args desktop=off
$ cpu start
4 of 4 processors in use
@screenshot 1920x1080 text
$& display test
@screenshot 1920x1080 bars
> x
$wait
color bars on the screen: press Enter to go on
~ ^drawing the whole screen again took \d+\.\d ms$
@screenshot 1920x1080 text
$ display speed
~ ^drawing the whole screen again takes \d+\.\d ms \(best of 5\)$
~ ^of which copying to video memory: \d+\.\d ms$
$ echo still typing
still typing
@screenshot 1920x1080 text
